{"1-7":{"people":[{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":3,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"ephraim-h0669g","name":"Ephraim","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":2,"firstVerse":3},{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":5}],"places":[{"id":"ramoth-h7216h","name":"Ramoth","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"tabor-mount-h8396g","name":"Tabor Mount","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":1}],"words":[{"base":"H0669","lemma":"אֶפְרַ֫יִם","tr":"eph·ra·yim","gloss":"Ephraim","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":180},{"base":"H3782","lemma":"כָּשַׁל","tr":"ka·shal","gloss":"to stumble","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":62},{"base":"H7846","lemma":"שֵׂט","tr":"set","gloss":"rebellion","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H6258","lemma":"עַתָּ֫ה","tr":"at·tah","gloss":"now","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":433},{"base":"H6009","lemma":"עָמֹק","tr":"a·maq","gloss":"be deep","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":9},{"base":"H8396","lemma":"תָּבוֹר","tr":"ta·vor","gloss":"(Mount) Tabor","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":10},{"base":"H2183","lemma":"זְנוּנִים","tr":"za·nun","gloss":"fornication","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":12},{"base":"H0589","lemma":"אֲנִי","tr":"a·ni","gloss":"I","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":874},{"base":"H3045","lemma":"יָדַע","tr":"ya·da","gloss":"to know","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":945},{"base":"H7568","lemma":"רֶ֫שֶׁת","tr":"re·shet","gloss":"net","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":22}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"HOS","chapter":4,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"My people consult their wooden idols, and their divining rods inform them. For a spirit of prostitution leads them astray and they have played the harlot against their God.","from":4},{"book":"HOS","chapter":7,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Israelʼs arrogance testifies against them, yet they do not return to the LORD their God; despite all this, they do not seek Him.","from":5},{"book":"HOS","chapter":9,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"The prophet is Ephraimʼs watchman, along with my God, yet the snare of the fowler lies on all his paths. Hostility is in the house of his God!","from":1},{"book":"PRO","chapter":1,"verse":28,"verseEnd":28,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Then they will call on me, but I will not answer; they will earnestly seek me, but will not find me.","from":6},{"book":"HOS","chapter":6,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"But they, like Adam, have transgressed the covenant; there they were unfaithful to Me.","from":7},{"book":"HOS","chapter":9,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"All their evil appears at Gilgal, for there I hated them. I will drive them from My house for the wickedness of their deeds. I will no longer love them; all their leaders are rebellious.","from":2},{"book":"MIC","chapter":6,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"With what shall I come before the LORD when I bow before the God on high? Should I come to Him with burnt offerings, with year-old calves?","from":6},{"book":"MIC","chapter":6,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"Would the LORD be pleased with thousands of rams, with ten thousand rivers of oil? Shall I present my firstborn for my transgression, the fruit of my body for the sin of my soul?","from":6}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]},"8-15":{"people":[{"id":"benjamin-h1144g","name":"Benjamin","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"ephraim-h0669g","name":"Ephraim","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":5,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":4,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"tiglath-pileser-h8407","name":"Tiglath-pileser","kind":"person","brief":"Assyrian king","count":1,"firstVerse":13}],"places":[{"id":"beth-aven-h1007","name":"Beth-aven","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"gibeah-h1390h","name":"Gibeah","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"ramah-h7414g","name":"Ramah","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"assyria-h0804g","name":"Assyria","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":13}],"words":[{"base":"H0669","lemma":"אֶפְרַ֫יִם","tr":"eph·ra·yim","gloss":"Ephraim","lang":"h","inPassage":6,"uses":180},{"base":"H4205","lemma":"מָזוֹר","tr":"ma·zor","gloss":"wound","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":3},{"base":"H3063","lemma":"יְהוּדָה","tr":"ye·hu·dah","gloss":"Judah","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":820},{"base":"H1007","lemma":"בֵּית אָ֫וֶן","tr":"bet a·ven","gloss":"Beth-aven","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":14},{"base":"H0589","lemma":"אֲנִי","tr":"a·ni","gloss":"I","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":874},{"base":"H3377","lemma":"יָרֵב","tr":"ya·rev","gloss":"`great`","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H7538","lemma":"רָקָב","tr":"ra·qav","gloss":"rottenness","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":5},{"base":"H9036","lemma":"כֶם","tr":"khem","gloss":"you","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":591},{"base":"H7826","lemma":"שַׁ֫חַל","tr":"sha·chal","gloss":"lion","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":7},{"base":"H0310","lemma":"אַחַר","tr":"a·char","gloss":"after","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":715}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"ISA","chapter":26,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":9,"source":"openbible","text":"O LORD, they sought You in their distress; when You disciplined them, they poured out a quiet prayer.","from":15},{"book":"DEU","chapter":4,"verse":29,"verseEnd":29,"votes":8,"source":"openbible","text":"But if from there you will seek the LORD your God, you will find Him if you seek Him with all your heart and with all your soul.","from":15},{"book":"DEU","chapter":4,"verse":31,"verseEnd":31,"votes":8,"source":"openbible","text":"For the LORD your God is a merciful God; He will not abandon you or destroy you or forget the covenant with your fathers, which He swore to them by oath.","from":15},{"book":"JER","chapter":29,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":8,"source":"openbible","text":"Then you will call upon Me and come and pray to Me, and I will listen to you.","from":15},{"book":"JER","chapter":29,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":8,"source":"openbible","text":"I will be found by you, declares the LORD, and I will restore you from captivity and gather you from all the nations and places to which I have banished you, declares the LORD. I will restore you to the place from which I sent you into exile.”","from":15},{"book":"PSA","chapter":78,"verse":34,"verseEnd":34,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"When He slew them, they would seek Him; they repented and searched for God.","from":15},{"book":"LEV","chapter":26,"verse":40,"verseEnd":40,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"But if they will confess their iniquity and that of their fathers in the unfaithfulness that they practiced against Me, by which they have also walked in hostility toward Me—","from":15},{"book":"LEV","chapter":26,"verse":42,"verseEnd":42,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"then I will remember My covenant with Jacob and My covenant with Isaac and My covenant with Abraham, and I will remember the land.","from":15}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":3}]}}